+## 2. Full-Spectrum Evaluations
+
+### R23 · Constitution portability: the Single Door rides a 60k-project standard — `adapt_cleanroom` → Issue #1702
+
+**Evidence trail (probed 2026-10-28):** the official agents.md site (live fetch) states the format is "used by
+over 60k open-source projects" and enumerates native consumers: OpenAI Codex, Cursor, GitHub Copilot coding
+agent, Google Gemini CLI, Google Jules, Devin (Cognition), Windsurf, Zed, VS Code, Aider, goose, opencode,
+RooCode, Ona, Warp, Amp, Kilo Code, Augment Code, Semgrep, Junie (JetBrains), Phoenix, UiPath Autopilot &
+Coded Agents, Factory. The site's thesis — "README for agents": a predictable, dedicated instruction surface —
+is precisely what `AGENTS.md` (The Single Door SSOT) already is for this federation, byte-for-byte compatible
+(plain Markdown, repo root). Corroborating: the Python Language Summit 2026 recap (python-insider,
+2026-09-30) lists a lightning talk titled "an AGENTS.md file for CPython" — even CPython is converging here.
+
+- **Pros:** zero-cost constitution propagation to every external contributor's toolchain; the 4 Universal
+  Invariants load without any bridge-side change; strengthens the "loop is the permission" doctrine because
+  foreign runtimes read the same rules the loop injects; documentation is a 1-file, 2-sentence change.
+- **Cons:** adopter toolchains interpret AGENTS.md loosely (advisory, not enforced); risk of over-promising
+  enforcement if docs imply tools *enforce* invariants — they only *carry* them.
+- **Risks:** nested per-satellite AGENTS.md files could drift from the root constitution — the issue pins
+  them as *references*, never forks; tool support for nested discovery varies and must be verified per
+  adopter before any implementation.
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** no `CLAUDE.md` / `.cursorrules` / duplicate instruction files that can drift from
+  AGENTS.md (Single Door = one SSOT; adapters import, never fork); no change to the Invariants or hub
+  architecture.
+- **Adoption path → Issue [#1702](https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/issues/1702).**
